      "id": "0004",
      "front": "How many $n$th roots does a non-zero complex number have, and how are they arranged on an Argand diagram?",
      "back": "There are $n$ distinct roots, equally spaced on a circle whose radius is the $n$th root of the modulus, with arguments separated by $\\frac{2\\pi}{n}$.",
      "keyPoints": [
        {
          "text": "n distinct roots",
          "mustInclude": true
        },
        {
          "text": "equally spaced on a circle",
          "mustInclude": true
        },
