          "text": "radius is the nth root of the modulus",
          "synonyms": [
            "|w|^(1/n)"
          ],
          "mustInclude": true
        },
        {
          "text": "arguments differ by 2\u03c0/n",
          "mustInclude": true
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "De Moivre applied backwards: the argument can be increased by any multiple of $2\\pi$ before dividing by $n$, and only the first $n$ choices give new roots.",
